    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "path": "docs/research/developer-dx-audit-2026-09-13.md",
      "issue": "The remaining React-authoring audit is incomplete. Imports, signature help, and definition navigation are listed as registered capabilities but have no current workflow probes or concrete limitations. JSX/bracket and multi-cursor authoring behavior also lacks the requested findings. Outcome 4 reduces the language-tooling gates to completion ordering and the false diagnostic defect.",
      "expected": "Complete the requested authoring capability matrix with current outcomes or specific verification limitations, and retain observable gates for the relevant authoring subflows.",
      "evidence": "Research report:118–125, :227–257 and :548–555; scripts/verify-dev-dx-audit.py:577–798. Independent adapter tests cover edit planning, not these UI workflows."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "path": "docs/research/developer-dx-audit-2026-09-13.md",
      "issue": "The completion-ranking conclusion exceeds its evidence. The report says the recorded top options started with Number, but JSON starts with CounterProbe. The helper captures options before typing the final 'ber', then accepts a later list without recording it. Accepting Number does not establish that number was offered and ranked below it; the VS Code comparison is also unsupported.",
      "expected": "Capture the settled list and selected item immediately before acceptance. Establish whether the primitive is absent or misranked, and support or qualify the VS Code comparison before prescribing a ranking fix.",
      "evidence": "scripts/verify-dev-dx-audit.py:669–693; dx-audit-results.json:81–87; research report:237–242, :453–458 and :552."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "path": "docs/research/developer-dx-audit-2026-09-13.md",
      "issue": "The upstream motion comparison contradicts itself: it says Zed has no buffer-scroll smoothing, then concludes both reference editors ship smooth scrolling as opt-in. The newly cited Zed implementations provide filenames and abbreviated revisions but omit the required exact supporting URLs.",
      "expected": "Separate caret and scrolling capabilities/defaults for each editor, reconcile the contradictory conclusion, and add exact revision permalinks for the inspected implementations.",
      "evidence": "Research report:319–351 versus :368–374. [VS Code editor options](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/vscode/main/src/vs/editor/common/config/editorOptions.ts) supports its own default-off settings, not the Zed conclusion."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "path": "docs/research/developer-dx-audit-2026-09-13.md",
      "issue": "Latency interpretation still contains unsupported claims. The document-level bubbling listener starts after CodeMirror's key handlers, so it does not bound total input handling as stated. The table labels the worst large-note long task approximately 106 ms, while JSON records 223 ms. Section 5 again calls median latency frame-competitive without a comparative measurement.",
